2026-11-26  Roman Senn  <roman.l.senn@gmail.com>

	* lib/session/usage-stats.js (emptyReplyNote), repl.js (chatRound): New.
	A reply with no text and no tool call prints a note with the finish
	reason, the tokens and where the answer may be (the reasoning, or the
	token limit). tests/test-empty-reply.js, run by smoke.sh.

	* lib/session/session-cache.js (addRoot, pickRoot, SESSION_SETTINGS),
	lib/session/session-log.js (SessionLog#cd), lib/tui/session-browser.js
	(detailLines), repl.js (main, /cd, persistState): state.json keeps
	startRoot, root and the chain roots of every /cd; a start goes on in
	the last directory, else the newest earlier one that exists, then the
	start one; /cd writes a CD line to session.log; the browser shows
	started in and moves. root is no longer one of the saved settings.
	tests/test-session-cache.js, tests/test-session-browser.js.

	* lib/project/resources.js (ownSockets, joinLws, lwsConnections): The
	connections come from LWSContext.sockets() (local, peer, protocol,
	buffered bytes) and are joined by local+peer address to the ss entries,
	which keep supplying the byte counters, rtt, kernel state, queues and
	unix sockets; an ss entry gains an lws field, a connected lws socket ss
	did not list is added as ESTAB. An lws.so without LWSContext.sockets
	leaves the plain ss result. tests/test-own-sockets.js, smoke.sh,
	doc/ARCHITECTURE.md, TODO.md follow.

	* lib/clients/openai-client.js (toolFields, chat, chatStream): New. A
	request carries tool_choice only together with tools; the last round of
	a tool loop (toolChoice none, no tools) made Cerebras answer HTTP 400.
	tests/test-provider-alias.js checks it.

	* lib/tui/rawcolor.js (lastLines), repl.js (chatRound onReasoning):
	New. The live reasoning panel colours only the last 6000 characters of
	the growing text; colouring all of it on every chunk cost about 0.6 s
	at 430 KB and blocked the loop in every chunk (lag stalls of 400 ms in
	the reasoning phase). tests/test-rawcolor.js checks lastLines.

	* BUGS: stream-dropped-in-long-reasoning.

	* lib/tui/session-browser.js: New. The session browser: a scrolling list
	with a highlighted row, the details of the highlighted session below,
	Enter/l loads, i inspects (splitHeights, scrollOffset, columnWidths,
	rowText, detailLines, transcriptText, SessionBrowser).

	* lib/session/session-cache.js (readSession): New. A session's state and
	conversation for the browser, read only.

	* lib/tui/chat-repl.js (ChatREPL#openSessionBrowser): New.

	* repl.js (/sessions, prepareSwitch, restartHook): /sessions opens the
	browser in the TUI (/sessions list prints the table); loading restarts
	the process with --name KEY and the saved model, without a harness
	check or --resume. ageText moved to the browser module.

	* lib/tui/pager.js (Pager#layout): setWidth() before setText(): the width
	was undefined, so a text in the plain pager was wrapped to one character
	per line.

	* tests/test-session-browser.js: New; tests/test-session-cache.js
	(readSession). smoke.sh runs them. doc/ARCHITECTURE.md "Session
	browser", README.md.

	* BUGS: smoke-leaves-sessions.

	* lib/ (all files): lib/ is regrouped into clients/, gateway/,
	failover/, tui/, project/, session/ and agent/, with the files shared
	by several areas (config, paths, match, look, ansi, palette, lag,
	events, run-command) staying in lib/. Every import, comment and doc
	mention was rewritten by move-modules; the import graph is the same
	before and after (265 edges).

	* smoke.sh, check-names.cjs, doc/ARCHITECTURE.md, README.md, TODO.md,
	doc/PLAN.md: lib/ files are found recursively; "Layout of lib/" is the
	record of the layout and the rule for new files.

	* lib/session-store.js (SessionStore): session.json is written to a
	.tmp file and renamed, carries version and updatedAt, and an unreadable
	file is renamed to session.json.corrupt (SessionStore#corrupt).

	* lib/session-cache.js (sessionKey, saveSessionState, SESSION_SETTINGS,
	pickSettings, applySettings, adoptLegacySession, listSavedSessions,
	pruneSessions): the key is the project (directory name and path hash),
	no longer the model; an old MODEL-HASH directory is adopted once;
	state.json is versioned and holds the session's settings; saved
	sessions can be listed and pruned.

	* lib/session-log.js (SessionLog#reply): the reply tag names the model
	instead of QWEN; the header comment says where the log is.

	* repl.js (parseArgs, main, sessionsCommand, persistState): the options
	the command line sets are recorded (opts.given); a plain start restores
	the session's saved settings, name and skipped models, and persistState
	writes them after every turn and command. New /sessions, --sessions and
	--prune-sessions. A corrupt session.json is reported.

	* tests/test-session-store.js, tests/test-session-cache.js: New.
	smoke.sh runs them (step 1g). doc/ARCHITECTURE.md "Sessions", README.md.

	* lib/pricing.js (PRICES, priceOf, estimateCost, fmtUsd): New. A price
	table (Cerebras) for endpoints that report no cost.

	* repl.js (main onMeta), lib/usage-stats.js (formatMeta, totals,
	summary): meta.costEst is the estimate of a reply without a reported
	cost; /last shows it and /usage sums it, both marked with a ~.

	* tests/test-pricing.js: New. smoke.sh runs it (step 1f).

	* lib/usage-stats.js (quotaWindows, quotaText), repl.js (/quota): New.
	/quota shows the x-ratelimit-* limits of the newest answer per window.

	* tests/test-quota.js: New. quotaText on Cerebras and OpenAI headers.

	* tests/test-provider-alias.js: New. resolveProvider and the client's
	env variable names.

	* smoke.sh: runs tests/test-provider-alias.js (step 1d).

	* lib/openai-client.js (PROVIDERS, resolveProvider, OpenAIClient): New.
	Curated provider aliases and openai:NAME read NAME_API_KEY/NAME_API_URL;
	the client takes apiUrlEnv and defaultBaseUrl.

	* repl.js (parseArgs): --provider accepts the curated aliases and
	openai:NAME; they need --model.

	* lib/availability.js (noteIpChange, ipLiftTally, reportChanges): one
	event says how many limits an address change lifted, per kind.

	* lib/usage-baseline.js (proxyLatency), repl.js (proxyText): /proxy shows
	what the proxy adds per platform (proxied against direct, 7 days).

	* repl.js (/model explore): the options --tier0 and --workers N.

	* lib/exploration.js (Exploration#liveSummary), repl.js (watchLive,
	refreshExplored, statusLines): the live state of the verified models is
	refreshed every 2 minutes while idle; the status bar shows usable/verified.

	* lib/ip-fix.js (ipProxyTargets, ipProxyReleases), repl.js (autoProxy):
	proxy policy: a keyed provider goes direct, its keys use the proxy only
	while it is limited per IP address and come off it 30 minutes after the
	limit (the 22 kilo keys of the old policy at startup).

	* lib/key-events.js (reportKeys): New. Key status changes as events,
	seen at every availability load; lib/freellm.js, lib/availability.js use it.

	* lib/persist.js (appendEvent, readEvents), repl.js: quota, failover and
	proxy events are kept in events.jsonl (30 days).

	* lib/proxy-probe.js (torCookie, newnym, exitAfterNewnym, newExit),
	repl.js: cookie authentication for a local Tor, NEWNYM waits out
	newnym-wait, /proxy exit asks for the new address until it changes.

	* lib/exploration.js (Exploration#cost, costText), repl.js: /model health
	and the sweep event show the probes sent in 24 h and their tokens.

	* lib/probe-context.js (needlesFor, buildProbe), lib/exploration.js
	(probeUsable, run), repl.js (exploreOrder): the tier 1 probe takes a seed
	and varies its three facts per run, against prompt caching.

	* lib/exploration.js (Exploration#current, fresh, run): a passed entry
	of the old three-prompt code (no v 3) is asked once more from scratch.

	* TODO.md (A3): lists the files to delete as they are now (strace.log*,
	perf.data).

	* lib/context-view.js (messageText, messageSelection, summarizeMessages,
	parseContextArgs), repl.js (main): New. The pure parts of /context and
	/log moved out of repl.js, with tests.

	* lib/availability.js (loadAvailabilityNow, SLOW_TABLES): the chain and
	routing tables are asked once a minute, { fresh: true } asks all; the
	result has keyCounts.

	* lib/fallback-trail.js (spentPlatforms), repl.js (onMeta): when every key
	of a platform ran out in the trail, its models are skipped together.

	* lib/persist.js (usageRow, appendUsage), lib/usage-baseline.js (baseline),
	repl.js (watchNet): the explore, standby and sub-agent clients log their
	requests in usage.jsonl with a label; the baseline counts turns from the
	unlabelled (main) rows only.

	* repl.js (localCandidate): the local fallback client reports to the
	status line and /usage (onMeta).

	* lib/lag.js (timed, startLagWatch): New. Loop-lag watch and timed
	sections; slow rows in lag.jsonl carry the callers (where).

	* lib/run-command.js (runCommand): output goes to an unlinked scratch
	file, not a pipe, so a descendant holding the pipe cannot block the loop.

	* lib/availability.js (loadAvailability, groupId, limitsText): concurrent
	loads share one request set, { fresh: true } reloads after a change;
	groupId memoised; limitsText sorts on a flag worked out once per row.

	* lib/model-status.js (modelStatusTable): sort keys worked out once per row.

	* repl.js (allModelNames, /model skip): the names are copied, not
	filtered and sorted per model (a 4.8 s stall on a spent provider).

	* lib/provider-fallback.js (resetMs, classify): the cool-down of a limit
	follows Retry-After or "Soonest cooldown reset ~3m".

	* lib/transcript-text.js (earliestReset), repl.js: the give-up panel ends
	with the earliest reset time.

	* repl.js (flushState): ratings, quota snapshot and cooldowns are written
	on exit, /restart, SIGTERM and SIGHUP.

	* lib/hop-line.js (hopLine), repl.js (servedVia): a single-model hop names
	the provider that served the spent model.

	* lib/gateway-report.js (reportText): /gateway status explains the
	degraded mode without a dashboard session.

	* tests/test-turn-repair.js: a tool that throws mid round.
